<SiteLayout title="People Who Know Your Family | Growing Kids" description="Meet the family behind Growing Kids and read published staff stories. Learn about local leadership and the people caring for children." breadcrumbs={[{name:"People Who Know Your Family",path:"/team/"}]}><section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><h1>People Who Know Your Family</h1><p class="intro">Growing Kids is family owned and locally led. Beth and Mike Garatoni started the company after becoming parents themselves, with a focus on children’s learning, safety and the peace of mind families need.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="/book-a-tour/">Schedule a Tour</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section cream"><div class="wrap split"><div data-care-reveal><h2>Accountability stays close to home.</h2><p>Mike remains involved in the daily life of Growing Kids. Decisions are made here, close to the families and teachers they affect. The path from a parent’s question to someone who can help is meant to be a short one.</p><p>That approach began with Beth and Mike’s own experience as parents. Their aim was to build a place where children could learn and grow while parents felt confident about their care.</p></div><img src="/images/growing-kids-family.webp" alt="Members of the Growing Kids family together" width="700" height="600" loading="lazy" data-shoot="replace"/></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap"><h2>Meet the people at your center.</h2><p>Start with your center’s director and teachers. They can talk through classroom routines, your child’s needs and what to expect as you get settled.</p><div class="review-note"><strong>Director and leadership profiles coming</strong>Names, photos, center assignments and verified years of service will be added as the current roster is confirmed.</div><ul class="link-list">{centers.map(c=><li><a href={c.location_path}>{c.name}</a></li>)}</ul></div></section><section class="section sage" id="staff-stories"><div class="wrap"><h2>Why our teachers stay.</h2><p>These stories come from staff accounts already published on the Growing Kids website. They reflect the experiences shared at that time.</p><blockquote class="quote">“The best part is teaching my Students new and exciting things daily. I think it's amazing how they grow and learn.”<cite>Shalena Mitchell · Chesterton Center</cite></blockquote><blockquote class="quote">“I have been able to grow within the company as well. I have gone from being a young preschool teacher to the office supervisor.”<cite>Mercedes Cobb · Published staff story</cite></blockquote><blockquote class="quote">“The support I receive to help me learn and grow as an educator brings me back everyday.”<cite>Nathan Evans · Published staff story</cite></blockquote><p class="review-note"><strong>Staff-story review</strong>Current roles, tenure, profile photos and reuse permissions need confirmation. These published stories do not establish current employment.</p><a class="button secondary" href="/careers/">Explore Careers</a></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Teachers keep learning, too.</h2><div><p>New teachers complete orientation and training in safety, health, classroom practices and center procedures. Growing Kids requires pediatric CPR and First Aid training and supports continued early childhood education.</p><a class="text-link" href="/curriculum/">Learn about our classroom approach</a></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>